<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zayn al-Din Ali Kuchuk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1168</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ali Kuchuk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zayn al-Din Ali Kuchuk, son of Begtegin, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> officer of the Zengid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imad-al-din-zengi">Imad al-Din Zengi</a>. From around 1144 he governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erbil">Erbil</a> and other towns in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and became the most powerful lord of the Zengid state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>. He founded the Begteginid dynasty of Erbil, which his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaffar-al-din-gokbori">Muzaffar al-Din Gökböri</a> later ruled.</p></div>
